# OctoAcme Collaboration Workflows

## Purpose
Define standard workflows and handoff patterns for common project scenarios to ensure smooth collaboration between roles.

---

## Workflow 1: Feature Development Lifecycle

### Phase 1: Ideation & Refinement (Product Manager + Developers)
1. Product Manager writes feature brief with problem, goals, success metrics
2. Product Manager + UX Designer conduct user research if needed
3. Product Manager and Developers meet for refinement
4. Developers raise technical feasibility concerns; PM adjusts scope if needed
5. UX Designer shares prototype or wireframe (if applicable)
6. Feature is added to backlog with clear acceptance criteria

### Phase 2: Development (Developers + QA/Testing + Scrum Master)
1. Feature is planned in sprint during sprint planning
2. Developers create feature branch and begin implementation
3. Developers and QA/Testing collaborate on test approach during sprint
4. Developers create pull request with:
   - Link to issue/story
   - Description of changes
   - Acceptance criteria checklist
   - Screenshots/demo instructions if UI-related
5. Peer review occurs; feedback is addressed
6. QA/Testing tests feature in staging environment
7. Feature is merged to main branch

### Phase 3: Acceptance & Release (Product Manager + QA/Testing + DevOps)
1. QA/Testing provides acceptance sign-off
2. Product Manager validates feature meets acceptance criteria (may do final QA)
3. Product Manager and DevOps coordinate release timing
4. DevOps deploys to production and verifies deployment
5. DevOps notifies Product Manager of successful deployment
6. Product Manager communicates release to stakeholders

### Phase 4: Post-Release (Product Manager + Data Analyst)
1. Data Analyst confirms success metrics are tracking correctly
2. Product Manager reviews early metrics and gathers user feedback
3. Product Manager logs issues for follow-up work
4. Action items are added to backlog for next iteration

