## Workflow 6: Cross-functional Collaboration (Design & Development)

### Phase 1: Design Discovery (UX Designer + Product Manager)
1. UX Designer conducts user research or reviews existing insights
2. UX Designer creates wireframes or mockups
3. UX Designer shares with Product Manager for feedback
4. UX Designer iterates based on feedback

### Phase 2: Design Validation (UX Designer + Developers)
1. UX Designer shares design with Developers for feasibility review
2. Developers identify technical constraints or opportunities
3. UX Designer and Developers discuss trade-offs
4. Design is finalized with input from both parties

### Phase 3: Implementation (Developers + UX Designer)
1. Developers implement design following design system
2. Developers share implementation screenshots with UX Designer
3. UX Designer validates pixel-perfect adherence if needed, or provides feedback on interaction
4. UX Designer approves implementation

### Phase 4: QA & Testing (QA/Testing + UX Designer)
1. QA/Testing executes test plan including usability checks
2. QA/Testing flags any usability issues or design deviations
3. UX Designer reviews issues and prioritizes fixes
4. Developers fix high-priority issues; lower-priority issues go to backlog

